What is __proto__ in JavaScript?

__proto__ = a getter/setter that lets you access an object's internal [[Prototype]].
That’s it.
It shows from which object this object is inheriting.
🧩 Think of it like a parent pointer
Every JS object secretly has:
[[Prototype]]
But you can’t access that directly.
So JavaScript gives:
__proto__
to view/change it.
✅ Basic Example

const animal = {
  eats: true
};

const dog = {};

dog.__proto__ = animal;

console.log(dog.eats);


Output:
true


Why?

JS checks:

dog → not found
dog.__proto__ → animal → found


This is prototype inheritance.

🔥 IMPORTANT: __proto__ is NOT the same as .prototype

Interviewers LOVE this confusion.

⭐ .prototype

✔ belongs to constructor functions

function User(){}
User.prototype

⭐ __proto__

✔ belongs to EVERY object

const obj = {}
obj.__proto__

🎯 Golden interview line:

.prototype is for functions, __proto__ is for objects.

Memorize this.

🏗 What happens with new
function User(){}
const u = new User();


Internally:

u.__proto__ === User.prototype


TRUE.

Interview classic question.

🧪 Proof:
function A(){}
const a = new A();

console.log(a.__proto__ === A.prototype);


✔ true

⚠️ VERY IMPORTANT (modern JavaScript rule)
🚨 __proto__ is considered legacy.

You SHOULD NOT use it in production.

Use:

Object.getPrototypeOf(obj)
Object.setPrototypeOf(obj, proto)


Interviewers like hearing this.

🧠 Why __proto__ exists at all?

For:

✔ debugging
✔ legacy browser support
✔ prototype inspection

Not for normal coding.

🔍 How property lookup works with __proto__

When you run:

obj.name


JS internally does:

check obj
check obj.__proto__
check obj.__proto__.__proto__
...
until null


This is the prototype chain.

🧬 Real chain example
const arr = [1,2,3];


Chain:

arr
arr.__proto__ === Array.prototype
Array.prototype.__proto__ === Object.prototype
Object.prototype.__proto__ === null


End of chain = null

Always.

⚠️ Interview Trap Questions
🚨 Trap 1

Is __proto__ standard?

Answer:

👉 It exists in modern JS but is legacy — use Object methods instead.

🚨 Trap 2

Do primitives have __proto__?

Yes (temporarily boxed).

"hello".__proto__ === String.prototype


TRUE.

This impresses interviewers.

🚨 Trap 3

Can you delete __proto__?

No — it's accessor on Object.prototype.

